{"claim_type":"fact","confidence":{"factors":["source: primary","verified: webfetch"],"score":0.95},"entity_ids":["ent_howard2021safe"],"evidence_ids":["ev_experimentation_advanced_0001"],"id":"claim_experimentation_advanced_0001","record_type":"claim","status":"active","text":"Howard, Ramdas, McAuliffe & Sekhon (2021) \u2014 derives time-uniform, nonparametric, nonasymptotic confidence sequences. Width converges to zero with explicit error bounds. Foundational for modern valid-anytime A/B testing inference.","topic":"experimentation_advanced"}
{"claim_type":"fact","confidence":{"factors":["source: primary","verified: webfetch"],"score":0.95},"entity_ids":["ent_johari2015always"],"evidence_ids":["ev_experimentation_advanced_0002"],"id":"claim_experimentation_advanced_0002","record_type":"claim","status":"active","text":"Johari, Pekelis & Walsh (2015 arXiv) \u2014 frames sequential analysis of A/B tests around the \"peeking\" problem. Provides always-valid p-values and CIs robust to continuous monitoring. KDD 2017 conference version \"Peeking at A/B Tests\" includes additional co-author Koomen.","topic":"experimentation_advanced"}
{"claim_type":"fact","confidence":{"factors":["source: primary","verified: webfetch"],"score":0.95},"entity_ids":["ent_eckles2017design"],"evidence_ids":["ev_experimentation_advanced_0003"],"id":"claim_experimentation_advanced_0003","record_type":"claim","status":"active","text":"Eckles, Karrer & Ugander (2017) \u2014 evaluates methods for designing + analyzing randomized experiments in networks (social, marketplace) to reduce bias from interference. Published Journal of Causal Inference.","topic":"experimentation_advanced"}
{"claim_type":"fact","confidence":{"factors":["source: primary","verified: webfetch"],"score":0.95},"entity_ids":["ent_bojinov2022design"],"evidence_ids":["ev_experimentation_advanced_0004"],"id":"claim_experimentation_advanced_0004","record_type":"claim","status":"active","text":"Bojinov, Simchi-Levi & Zhao (Management Science 2023) \u2014 derives optimal switchback designs under different carryover-effect assumptions. Applications: ride-hailing, online marketplaces.","topic":"experimentation_advanced"}
{"claim_type":"fact","confidence":{"factors":["source: primary","verified: webfetch"],"score":0.95},"entity_ids":["ent_li2010contextual"],"evidence_ids":["ev_experimentation_advanced_0005"],"id":"claim_experimentation_advanced_0005","record_type":"claim","status":"active","text":"Li, Chu, Langford & Schapire (WWW 2010) \u2014 models personalized news article recommendation as a contextual bandit problem. Yahoo! Front Page Today Module deployment: 12.5% click lift vs context-free bandit. Foundational contextual-bandit paper.","topic":"experimentation_advanced"}
{"claim_type":"fact","confidence":{"factors":["source: primary","verified: webfetch"],"score":0.95},"entity_ids":["ent_athey2019generalized"],"evidence_ids":["ev_experimentation_advanced_0006"],"id":"claim_experimentation_advanced_0006","record_type":"claim","status":"active","text":"Athey, Tibshirani & Wager (Annals of Statistics 2019) \u2014 generalized random forests framework with causal forests as a special case for HTE estimation. Adaptive weighting based on forest-derived heterogeneity.","topic":"experimentation_advanced"}
{"claim_type":"fact","confidence":{"factors":["source: primary","verified: webfetch"],"score":0.95},"entity_ids":["ent_chapelle2011empirical"],"evidence_ids":["ev_experimentation_advanced_0007"],"id":"claim_experimentation_advanced_0007","record_type":"claim","status":"active","text":"Chapelle & Li (NeurIPS 2011) \u2014 empirical evaluation of Thompson sampling on simulated + real bandit data. Argues Thompson sampling should be a standard baseline.","topic":"experimentation_advanced"}
{"claim_type":"fact","confidence":{"factors":["source: primary","verified: webfetch"],"score":0.95},"entity_ids":["ent_gronau2019informed"],"evidence_ids":["ev_experimentation_advanced_0008"],"id":"claim_experimentation_advanced_0008","record_type":"claim","status":"active","text":"Gronau et al. (2019 arXiv) \u2014 Bayesian inference framework for A/B testing with informed priors. Prior + posterior probability formulation; discusses decision thresholds.","topic":"experimentation_advanced"}
{"claim_type":"fact","confidence":{"factors":["source: primary","verified: webfetch"],"score":0.95},"entity_ids":["ent_kohavi2014seven"],"evidence_ids":["ev_experimentation_advanced_0009"],"id":"claim_experimentation_advanced_0009","record_type":"claim","status":"active","text":"Kohavi, Deng, Longbotham & Xu (KDD 2014) \u2014 seven rules of thumb derived from experimentation at Amazon, Booking.com, LinkedIn, multiple Microsoft properties. Covers ramping at 1% increments, sample-size choice, organizational adoption, OEC selection.","topic":"experimentation_advanced"}
